From 998edb0f14d60a7a97c6075e4b6d269286a3a820 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:06:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: unify client creation into one entry point (Phase 6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the two separate "new client" wizards with one minimal,
name-only creation flow — real per-worker setup (Pin-Down, Identity
Setup, or both) happens on the client's own page afterward, same as an
engagement created through Teammates chat already works.

- New POST /api/engagements/minimal-create, calling the same
  createMinimalEngagement chat's create_client tool already uses.
- /dashboard/engagements/new replaced with a single client-name field
  (was a 5-step Showtime-only wizard: offer/stack/credentials/confirm/
  launch).
- /dashboard/reputation-manager/new replaced with a redirect to the
  unified page (verified zero field gap: same IdentityGraphForm/
  saveRepIdentityGraphIntake as bridges/rep-onboarding).
- engagements/page.tsx's two product-conditional links simplified to
  the one unified URL.

Closed the real field gaps found in the old Showtime wizard before
retiring it, so nothing is lost by deferring setup off the create step:
- slack_webhook_url was writable only via engagement setup — added to
  the PATCH allowlist and to EditStackSettings' new Notifications
  section (blocking: Leak Map/Crisis Response alert delivery had no
  other UI).
- hosting/SMS/ad-data platform credentials had no UI anywhere outside
  the old wizard — added to UpdateCredentialsForm and both its callers
  (blocking: those fields would've become permanently unreachable).
- 8 more fields (target/recovery list & workflow ids, activecampaign
  base url, hubspot portal id, long-term nurture list id, sms a2p/
  compliance-footer fields, ad data cohort id, publish domain, booking
  standing link, brief landing destination) added to the PATCH
  allowlist with matching enum validation where applicable.

The old wizard's step components (steps/, draft-storage.ts,
use-draft-persistence.ts, etc.) are left in place, unrouted rather than
deleted — form-fields.tsx in the same directory is still a real
dependency of identity-graph-form.tsx, and the rest weren't
exhaustively traced for zero remaining references. Follow-up cleanup,
not done here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
